<details><summary>Click to reveal the quantum caveat</summary>
A universal linear map cannot send every $x$ to $x\otimes x$: linearity omits the cross terms created by tensoring $x+y$ with itself. This [no-cloning theorem](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No-cloning_theorem) concerns copying, not algorithmic undecidability.
</details>
